Spec: Heat points

Purpose:
  The weighted points the overview heatmap draws, taken along ride outlines.

Owns:
  ./heat_points.dart
  /test/domain/heat_points_test.dart

References:
  /docs/decisions/0001-ride-outlines.md
  /lib/domain/ride_outline.sdd

Must:
  @HeatPoints.along places points at equal arc length of `30` m along an outline, starting at its first point
    and ending on its last, so a longer ride gets more points.
  An outline shorter than `30` m gives its first and last point.
  An outline with fewer than two points gives none.
  Points keep the ride order and carry no weight other than `1`.
  Between two outline points the heat points follow the short arc, also across `±180` longitude, and their
    longitudes stay within `-180` to `180` (#100).

Must not:
  Round to a grid or merge points of different rides; the map layer adds overlapping heat.

Example:
  a straight `100` m outline: points at `0`, `30`, `60`, `90` and `100` m
